Cards in US English on first aid that teach how the body works and what standard terms mean (what CPR stands for, why the recovery position keeps the airway open, what a tourniquet does, what shock means), never instructions to follow in an emergency, doses, or treatment advice. Guideline numbers that change between editions (compression rates and depths, ratios) are a never-write. Fewer than 10 cards is fine. Score accuracy at most 6 for any card that tells the learner what to do for an injury or illness.